OL,3,GNEWSARise in permanent exclusions in
OL,4,Aborough's schools
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe number of pupils who were
OL,7,Fpermanently excluded from schools
OL,8,Facross a borough in the last academic
OL,9,Fyear has risen by more than 20%,
OL,10,Ffigures show.
OL,12,FIn the year 2025/26 there were 89
OL,13,Fpermanent exclusions in Redcar and
OL,14,FCleveland schools, 16 more than the
OL,15,Fprevious year.
OL,17,FA report presented to the local
OL,18,Fauthority by Labour councillor Bill
OL,19,FSuthers said the rise was due to
OL,20,F"persistent disruptive behaviour" as
OL,21,Fwell as an increase in physical
OL,22,Fassaults and threats of assault.
OL,23,APub: 26-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NE Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
